From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0141: battery from the MAX1720x fuel gauge (bluemax=1 log, 2 publish)

The Pixel 3's gauge is a Maxim MAX1720x on qupv3_se12_i2c (i2c@a90000,
Linux bus 4) at 0x36/0x0b, not the PMI8998 FG that 0130 reads. Read it
with the touch driver's bit-banged I2C, now exported as
blueline_bbi2c_open()/_xfer() (touch unchanged in behaviour), on GPIO
49/50. Read-only: register pointers only, no register writes.

bluemax=1: log the gauge (once at start, and every bluebatt=1 refresh).
bluemax=2 (with bluebatt=1): publish its %, mV, mA, temperature,
FullCapRep/RepCap, cycle count and TTE/TTF; 0130's charger/plug state stays.
bluemax_rsense=N overrides Rsense (10 uOhm units; default nRSense, else 500).

